/-!
# Holomorphic Fricke fractions are integral over K[j]

Theorem statement: `WLight.exists_monicRel_j_K_of_mdifferentiable_frickeQuotient`
(`5921eedf-dc5b-56e0-b86a-16413b6fdb7e`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `05135d8b-3e8b-5f8d-9ab7-6c2b657286b1`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix $N$ with $N \neq 0$, and an assignment $L$ of period pairs to points of the upper half-plane
with $(L\tau).\omega_1 = \tau$ and $(L\tau).\omega_2 = 1$. Let $W$ be a family of functions indexed
by $v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$ pinned by $W_v(\tau) = (2\pi i)^{-2}\,\wp_{L\tau}\big((v_0\tau +
v_1)/N\big)$, where $v_0, v_1$ are the canonical integer representatives, let $\mathrm{fricke}$ be
pinned by $\mathrm{fricke}_v(\tau) = -\big(E_4(\tau)E_6(\tau)/\Delta(\tau)\big)/2592 \cdot
W_v(\tau)$, and let $jf$ be pinned by $jf(\tau) = E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$. Let $K \subseteq
\mathbb{C}$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by $e^{2\pi i/N}$. Let $G
: \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be holomorphic, and let $P_0, Q_0$ be polynomials over $K$ in variables
indexed by $\mathrm{Option}\,\{v \in (\mathbb{Z}/N)^2 : v \neq 0\}$; write $\tilde P_0, \tilde Q_0 :
\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ for their evaluations after pushing the coefficients into $\mathbb{C}$,
sending the distinguished variable to $jf$ and the variable $v$ to $\mathrm{fricke}_v$. Assume
$\tilde Q_0 \neq 0$ in the algebra of functions $\mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ and $G \cdot \tilde Q_0
= \tilde P_0$. Then there exist $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and polynomials $p_i \in \mathbb{C}[X]$ for $i <
d$, all of whose coefficients lie in $K$, such that $G(\tau)^d + \sum_{i<d} p_i(jf(\tau))\,G(\tau)^i
= 0$ for every $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$.

This is the arithmetic refinement, from $\mathbb{C}$-coefficients to coefficients in
$\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)$, of the statement that a holomorphic fraction of polynomial expressions in $j$
and the Fricke functions of level $N$ is integral over $K[j]$; it rests on the modularity and
$q$-expansion properties of the Fricke functions together with the descent of linear independence
from $K$ to $\mathbb{C}$ for functions with $q$-expansion coefficients in $K$. It is used in the
construction of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_N)$-rational structures on spaces of modular and cusp forms of
level $N$, in particular for rationality of $q$-expansion coefficients of $\Gamma_1(N)$-forms.

